      "timestamp_raw": "Oct 25, 2024 12:17:15 GMT -5",
      "body_html": "L42x HCW F select clone, photos taken 10/25/24:<br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/54093209379_c071c9cfca_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/><img src=\"https://live.staticflickr.com/65535/54092877296_81f5ae3d84_z.jpg\" style=\"max-width: 100%;\"/><br/><br/>My Rod's favorite got really white this year, but it got so jacked up with spots that it's not worth photographing this season.  We had dense, foggy mornings when it was developing (the traps emerged earlier than many others for some reason), which explains all the blemishes, guess we'll have to wait till next year on that one!",
